# File: .env.example
# History: Version 0.3, October 17, 2026
# Program: Show the local configuration keys required by Docker Compose without including real credentials.
# Input: Two independently generated 64-character hexadecimal passwords and an optional owned HTTPS domain.
# Processing: Copy to .env, replace both password placeholders, and leave PUBLIC_SITE_URL empty for local-only use.
# Output: Local-only configuration consumed by Compose and ignored by Git.
POSTGRES_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
APP_DATABASE_PASSWORD=
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
